{
  "_minTimeoutMs_provenance": "t/3555: `minTimeoutMs: 0` on the fast-class reachable models (gemini/azure/openai flash/lite/mini, claude-haiku-4-5, groq llama/oss, deepseek-v4-flash) is a 0-BY-DEFAULT CLASS judgment (120s base timeout deemed sufficient by model class) — NOT a per-model measured latency. Two reachable models were individually reviewed to a real 300000 floor instead of 0: openai-gpt-5.5 (flagship base; its pro sibling is floored) and ollama-gemma4-e4b-it-q4-k-m (local inference, hardware-dependent cold-start). Per-model p99-latency validation of the zeros is tracked in t/3662. Do not read a 0 here as a measured value. zai-glm-5-3 / zai-glm-5-3-flash are 0 by MEASUREMENT, not class: every Z.AI call sends reasoning_effort low (lib/ai-client/providers/zai.ts), and a 46KB debate-brief prompt on glm-5.3 measured 21s at low effort vs 205s at provider-default effort (2026-10-02). Raise the floor again if that effort setting is ever removed. claude-haiku-5-5 (t/4086) is floored at 300000, NOT the fast-class 0 that claude-haiku-4-5 uses: it is a 5.x model with adaptive thinking + effort whose reasoning can exceed the 120s base, so it is floored like the other 5.x Claude models (sonnet-5-5, opus-5), not treated as fast-class. Per-model p99-latency validation (t/3662) would refine this.",
